{
    "background_story": "Pedro was a charming, affable gentleman with a penchant for getting into absurd, comedic misadventures. A devotee of the works of P.G. Wodehouse, he often found himself emulating the likes of Bertie Wooster, navigating the complexities of high society with a mixture of wit, luck, and haplessness. Pedro's own life was a series of Jeeves-esque escapades, as he careened from one ridiculous situation to the next, often due to his own well-meaning but misguided attempts to help his friends and acquaintances. His exploits became the stuff of legend among his social circle, with tales of his mishaps and mayhem being retold and embellished at dinner parties and country estates. Despite the chaos he often created, Pedro's good nature and Wodehouse-esque charm always managed to see him through, earning him a reputation as the most lovable, if slightly befuddled, gentleman of his acquaintance.",
